---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaStrip from '../components/CtaStrip.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Lozen Advisory | Board and CFO AI Governance Advisory" description="Lozen Advisory helps boards, CFOs, legal, and risk leaders evaluate AI accountability, authorization, and financial exposure.">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="grid-bg"></div>
  <div class="wrap inner">
    <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; About</div>
    <span class="pill">Our story &amp; mission</span>
    <h1>On a mission to make AI accountability governable</h1>
    <p class="sub">Lozen Advisory exists to make AI accountability visible and actionable. We turn complex governance, authorization, and human-attribution risk into clear decisions for boards, CFOs, legal, and risk leaders.</p>
    
  </div>
</section>

<section id="main">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Who we are</span>
      <h2 class="h2">From institutional analysis to board advisory</h2>
      <p>Lozen Advisory is a founder-led advisory firm focused on the governance and financial exposure created by AI-assisted decisions.</p>
      <p>We help leadership determine who owns the decision, what the operating record can prove, and where accountability breaks down before the organization is forced to answer after an incident.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="checklist" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Board- and CFO-facing AI governance analysis</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Proprietary accountability frameworks</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Legislation-to-enterprise risk translation</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Focused executive and organizational briefings</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head"><span class="eyebrow">What we believe</span><h2 class="h2">Our values</h2></div>
    <div class="values">
      <div class="value reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div><h3>Clarity over abstraction</h3><p>We turn complex AI governance problems into decisions leadership can act on.</p></div>
      <div class="value reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></div><h3>Accountability before exposure</h3><p>We identify where authority, evidence, and financial ownership are unclear before failure assigns them after the fact.</p></div>
      <div class="value reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg></div><h3>Evidence over assurance</h3><p>We examine what the operating record can prove, not what policy language assumes.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head"><span class="eyebrow">Our journey</span><h2 class="h2">How we got here</h2></div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="tl reveal"><div class="yr">Institutional analysis</div><h3>Turning data into decisions</h3><p>Founder Akilah E. Kamaria built her career using data to support decisions at scale inside demanding institutions.</p></div>
      <div class="tl reveal"><div class="yr">Research and standards</div><h3>Finding the gaps inside the record</h3><p>Her work included research on race and gender discrimination and foundational contributions to cybersecurity information-sharing standards.</p></div>
      <div class="tl reveal"><div class="yr">2025</div><h3>Lozen Advisory founded</h3><p>The firm was created to address the governance and measurement failures conventional systems were not built to see.</p></div>
      <div class="tl reveal"><div class="yr">Today</div><h3>Board-ready AI risk advisory</h3><p>Lozen Advisory now helps boards, CFOs, legal, and risk leaders evaluate accountability, authorization, and financial exposure across AI-assisted work.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head"><span class="eyebrow">The team</span><h2 class="h2">People who do this every day</h2></div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="member reveal"><div class="av"><img src="/founder-daniel-carter.png" alt="Akilah E. Kamaria" /></div><div class="nm">Daniel Carter</div><div class="rl">Founder &amp; Lead Consultant</div></div>
      <div class="member reveal"><div class="av"><img src="/team-aisha-morgan.png" alt="Aisha Morgan" /></div><div class="nm">Aisha Morgan</div><div class="rl">Head of Market Research</div></div>
      <div class="member reveal"><div class="av"><img src="/team-raj-kapoor.png" alt="Raj Kapoor" /></div><div class="nm">Raj Kapoor</div><div class="rl">Logistics &amp; Compliance Lead</div></div>
      <div class="member reveal"><div class="av"><img src="/team-elena-lopez.png" alt="Elena Lopez" /></div><div class="nm">Elena Lopez</div><div class="rl">Buyer Relations Manager</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<CtaStrip
  title="Is your board receiving enough evidence to govern AI risk?"
  description="Request a briefing for board, CFO, legal, or risk leadership on accountability gaps, human-attribution exposure, and what the operating record can actually prove."
  primaryHref="/request-briefing/"
  primaryLabel="Request a Board Briefing →"
  secondaryHref="/webinar/"
  secondaryLabel="Attend the Webinar"
  paddedTop={false}
/>
</BaseLayout>
